Part 1: Design (on paper or in a comment)

A small library needs to track:

books (title, author, year)
members (name, email)
loans (which member borrowed which book, and when)

Decide:

What tables you need and what columns each has
The primary key of each table
Which column is a foreign key, and what it points to
Which relationship each pair of tables has (one-to-many or many-to-many)

Part 2: Build it in Python with sqlite3

Write a function create_tables(conn) that creates your tables.
Write a function add_books(conn, books) that takes a list of tuples like ("Dune", "Frank Herbert", 1965) and uses a for loop to insert each one.
Write a function get_books_by_author(conn, author) that returns all books by that author.
Add 4-5 books, then call the third function and print the result.

